  "worked_solution": "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},\u2026,{x}_{n},$ then the mean is denoted by $\\overset{\u2015}{x}$ and is given by the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\overset{\u2015}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=15$ and ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{x}_{i}=91,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\u2015}{x} & =\\frac{1}{15}\\cdot 91\u22486.1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we have rounded our answer to one decimal place.",
